se,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-18T15:04:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T15:09:39Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.dev [220b0b2f7], 4.6.stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop - Intel i7-12700H (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nMoved here from https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14488, since this is a bug and not a missed feature.\n\nCurrently, no warning is thrown when a local variable/constant/enum shadows a global constant/enum in `@GDScript` or `@GlobalScope`, even though the latter are being shadowed when parsed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen this script in the script editor:\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name _Main\nextends Node\n\nvar PI = -10 # Missing warning.\nvar OK = -20 # Missing warning.\nenum Error { # Missing warning.\n\tOK = -30 # Missing warning.\n}\nvar Side = -40 # Missing warning.\nvar MouseButtonMask # Missing warning.\nvar number = -60 # No warning.\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117567/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://